@page "/events/tutorials"

<TutorialDetail>
<p>Step-by-step guides for using <code>RForge.Blazor.Events</code> in a Blazor app. They assume you already know Blazor components, dependency injection and render modes, and explain only what's specific to the hub.</p>

<p>Start with <strong>Setup</strong>. After that, each tutorial stands alone: it has its own small example, so you can jump straight to the topic you need.</p>

<div class="table-container">
    <table class="table is-striped">
        <thead>
            <tr><th>#</th><th>Tutorial</th><th>You'll learn</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var tutorial in EventsTutorialList.All)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td>@tutorial.Number</td>
                    <td><a href="@tutorial.Url">@tutorial.Title</a></td>
                    <td>@tutorial.Description</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 id="two-conventions-used-everywhere">Two conventions used everywhere</h2>

<p>Every event-aware component in these tutorials follows two rules. <a href="/events/tutorials/01-setup">Setup</a> explains why.</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>The <code>.razor</code> file starts with <code>@@inherits RfEventComponent</code>.</strong></li>
<li><strong><code>[Subscribe]</code> and <code>[UseState]</code> members live in the code-behind (<code>.razor.cs</code>)</strong>, never in an <code>@@code</code> block.</li>
</ol>

<p>Each code block starts with a comment giving the <strong>file path</strong> it belongs in, for example <code>// MyApp.Client/Features/Counter/CounterState.cs</code>. The paths follow the <a href="/events/tutorials/01-setup#1-lay-out-the-project">recommended project layout</a>.</p>

<h2 id="see-also">See also</h2>

<ul>
<li><a href="/events/details">Events overview</a>: install, basic usage and the runnable examples.</li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/Rumhyek/RForge/blob/main/docs/events/design/index.md">Design specification</a>: why the library works the way it does.</li>
</ul>
</TutorialDetail>
